

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 10

                                  FOR

                                II KAHN







          Lorenzo Cammoranesi
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Winter gave way to spring, and Kahn prepared to carry out his urgent 
assignments.  He read the Manual of Speedy Marches, and then it crumbled to 
dust.  His skill in Marches rose by 1 level.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
invaded Bir Nzaran, hoping to subjugate that province owned by II Kahn and 
made up of great Deserts.  Odysseus (#97)'s forces encountered little 
opposition in Bir Nzaran and Odysseus there established our rule.  Odysseus 
leads approximately 2 Bowmen, 4 Dragons, 2 Eagles and 1 Trolls.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  Kahn cancelled his move to the 
Angel Sea in order to fight for the province of Ravenwood.  So, Kahn worked 
on his Tactics but was frustrated in his self-improvement efforts.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Ravenwood, a 
Forest area owned by II Kahn.  Odysseus (#97) commanded the invading armies. 
The defending forces were led by Kahn.  The armies were drawn up into lines 
of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Ravenwood (1102):

