  DEFENDING ARMY

  Odysseus led a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.  II Kahn stood 
ready at the head of his thousands.
  Odysseus was unlucky this day, for many of his skirmishers became 
scattered in a swamp.  Kahn thus gained a significant edge.  As the 
desperate battle developed, the tactical wit of Kahn and Odysseus seemed 
evenly matched.

  Out on the right outside flank, the Crack 334th Bowmen faced the Veteran 
188th Bowmen.  The 91st Dragons soared over the 188th Bowmen and attacked 
without mercy.  The 91st Dragons were decimated by the bolts loosed by those 
dangerous Bowmen.  On this battleground, the 188th Bowmen expected to have 
the advantage because they had constructed prepared defenses, but were 
chagrined to find out that their enemy had done the same.  The 334th Bowmen 
battled with the 188th Bowmen and managed to make some progress.
  Within the interior lines, the Veteran 198th Trolls faced the Veteran 
220th Light Cavalry.  The 123rd Eagles soared over the 220th Light Cavalry 
and attacked them.  In this area, some soldiers of the 198th Trolls noticed 
the presence of an encampment of trollops behind their opponents, so they 
lustily concentrated their efforts to break through.
  But might defeat now be snatched from the jaws of victory?  The commander 
of the 220th Light Cavalry decided on a charge.  He moved to the front and 
shouted "Smash the cowards!"   and the 220th Light Cavalry charged 
valiantly.  Even with the 220th Light Cavalry's good luck, the 198th Trolls 
battled with the 220th Light Cavalry and gradually shoved them back.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 206th Dragons faced the Veteran 218th 
Legion.  The 206th Dragons swooped down on the 218th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  The 102nd Eagles soared over the 218th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  On this field, the soldiers of the 218th Legion were delayed 
by a muddy field.  The 206th Dragons fought with the 218th Legion and moved 
ahead slowly, battled for every foot of their advance.
  Out on the left flank, the Veteran 333rd Bowmen faced the 16th Legion, who 
were blessed by a band of priests sent by the League of Pagan Clerics, which 
aroused them to a fanatical zeal.  The 249th Dragons swooped down on the 
16th Legion and attacked without mercy.  Here, an officer of the 16th Legion 
perceived a gap in the enemy lines which had opened when they moved around a 
wide rock formation.  Charging into the gap, the 16th Legion gained a 
considerable advantage.
  But would victory yet be snatched from the jaws of defeat?  The 333rd 
Bowmen used wide-headed arrows to slash apart the enemy's catapult engines.  
The 333rd Bowmen fought the 16th Legion and plowed into their opponents.
  The forces of Odysseus broke through the lines of their enemy and were 
victorious.  The 334th Bowmen scattered the 188th Bowmen in all directions.  
The 333rd Bowmen destroyed the 16th Legion.  The 91st Dragons pursued the 
enemy and annihilated the 218th Legion.  The 102nd Eagles gave chase and 
demolished the 220th Light Cavalry.
  Odysseus's campaign accomplished the conquest of Ravenwood.
  Kahn's forces fought in a battle in Rejaf, but a foreign general commanded 
it.  The battle is in the General Intelligence Report.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  Kahn attempted an 
illegal move.  He tried to move from Ravenwood to Kildare, a non-adjacent 
province.  Instead, Kahn moved into the Angel Sea.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into the fall.  Kahn attempted an 
illegal move.  He tried to move from the Angel Sea to the Jellyfish Sea, a 
non-adjacent province.  Instead, Kahn rode into Mare Ionium.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  Kahn could not cast Tornado on 
the Dolphin Sea because Kahn needed to be in or next to the target province. 
Instead, Kahn invented nothing in his sagely experiments.

  Sredna ordered the 87th Skeletal Garrison, the 88th Skeletal Garrison and 
the 214th Skeletal Fleet to remain encamped in Sherwood with Kahn.  Sredna 
went back to Valhalla, having done his best to execute his assignments.

  Thus endeth the adventures of II Kahn for this year.


  Kahn treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Kahn treated with his ally 
Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Kahn treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Kahn 
treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Kahn treated with his ally Giovanna 
(#7).  Kahn treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Kahn treated with his ally 
Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Kahn's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 16 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  6
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Kahn was left with 36 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Sredna
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to fragrant spring.  I cast a Part Sea spell and 
the waters of the Angel Sea were magically parted.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I moved into Peachwood.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer came.  I rode into Sherwood.
  During fall, I cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 87th Skeletal Garrison, 
the 88th Skeletal Garrison and the 214th Skeletal Fleet arose from the 
graves of the dead!

  In Sherwood, II Kahn brought to bay Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
(#1).  Sredna's forces conquered Sherwood without any major engagements.  
Sherwood was found to have a tax base of 10 gold.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I attempted an illegal move.  
I was ordered to move from Sherwood to Bronzeleaf, but it is illegal to move 
naval forces from one non-sea province to another.  Instead, I discovered 
nothing in my sagely experiments.
  I ordered the 87th Skeletal Garrison, the 88th Skeletal Garrison and the 
214th Skeletal Fleet to remain encamped in Sherwood with Kahn.  I went back 
to Valhalla, having done my best to execute my assignments.


  Thy humble servant,   Sredna


From: Frodo, Squire to Hawkins
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter melted into fragrant spring.  Hawkins's Oratory spell 
fizzled and Hawkins was left with his face covered with psycho-kinetic 
slime.
  During early summer, Hawkins cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory 
armies were formed for Hawkins.
  Midsummer's night came and went and a pleasant late summer came.  Hawkins 
practiced his Psychic Magic diligently for many weeks, but could make no 
significant progress.
  During fall, Hawkins could not recruit Light Cavalry and Light Cavalry in 
Sherwood because Kahn does not own that province, and mercenaries weren't 
available.  Instead, Hawkins practiced his Illusions well but could not 
improve his Illusions.
  The fall season cooled into a frigid early winter.  Hawkins rode into 
Gnarlia.

  Thy humble servant,   Frodo, Squire to Hawkins


