GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1):
  In early summer, Guerin (#18) was in command of the invading armies.  The 
defenders were led by Rolando (#55).
  In late summer, Kajaani was hit by a plague.

  In early winter, soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the 
Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)ian empire marched on the Plain province of Kajaani, a 
land garrisoned by the soldiers of Giovanna (#7).  Guerin (#18) commanded 
the invading armies.  The defenders were commanded by Giovanna (#7).  The 
host of the attacking Kingdom was defeated and forced out of Kajaani.
  In late summer, Odysseus (#97) flew over to Peachwood.
  In early winter, the Plain terrain of Kajaani was magically made to appear 
as Forest.

Kingdom of Giovanna (#7):
  In late summer, Kajaani was hit by a plague.
  In early winter, the Plain terrain of Kajaani was magically made to appear 
as Forest.
  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)ian 
empire marched on the Plain province of Kajaani, a land garrisoned by the 
soldiers of Giovanna (#7).  Guerin (#18) commanded the invading armies.  The 
defenders were commanded by Giovanna (#7).  The host of the attacking 
Kingdom was defeated and forced out of Kajaani.
  From Kahn:  In early summer, Rolando (#55) marched into Rejaf from Kajaani 
to defend Rejaf against its would-be conquerors.
  A great host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Desert province of Rejaf, 
held by II Kahn.  Guerin (#18) was in command of the invading armies.  The 
defenders were led by Rolando (#55).  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

