  DEFENDING ARMY

  Guerin (#18) commanded a host of loyal soldiers.  Rolando (#55) marched 
with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  Tiffany (#87) stood 
ready at the head of her thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Guerin (#18)'s men, ill-supplied in the tortuous desert 
campaign, suffered from thirst.  Guerin was unlucky this time, for supplies 
were running low and some of his troops had to fight on empty stomachs.  On 
the other hand his clever tactical planning gave his side a clear advantage.

  Out on the right flank, the Elite 240th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 74th 
Camel Corps.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 74th Camel Corps 
and attacked without mercy.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 74th 
Camel Corps and cut them down like beanstalks.
  In the interior front, the Crack 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
20th Legion.  The 277th Eagles swooped down on the 20th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  In this sector, the 20th Legion's opponents were lined up in 
an upslope position.  But the 20th Legion charged them, and because there 
was no counter-charge, the 20th Legion shoved them off the crest and gained 
the upper hand.  In spite of the 20th Legion's good luck, the 110th Bowmen 
fought the 20th Legion and managed to make some measure of progress.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were inspired 
to fanatiscm by Guerin, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced 
the 21st Legion.  On this battleground, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen were 
slightly disrupted by a slippery patch of ground and they joined the fight 
at a tiny disadvantage.  Even so, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 21st 
Legion and gradually shoved them back.
  Within the interior lines, the Green 292nd Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the 244th Light Cavalry.  Here, the 292nd Skeletal Legion were 
inspired by the exhortations of an officer who bellowed "Do you want to be 
remembered as Heroes or despised as cowards?  Charge!  !  !"  Even with the 
292nd Skeletal Legion's good luck, the 292nd Skeletal Legion fought the 
244th Light Cavalry and were bent back by their pressure.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 241st Skeletal Bowmen faced the 239th 
Legion.  In this engagement, the contest was a straightforward bashing match 
determined by the courage of the men themselves in melee combat.  The 241st 
Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 239th Legion and the fighting here proved 
inconclusive.
  In the interior lines, the 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry were inspired to 
berserk fanatiscm by Guerin, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They 
were arrayed against the 230th Legion.  The Heavy Cavalry troops charged the 
230th Legion and they wavered under the initial impact.  Here, the 230th 
Legion had to go through a ford.  But their enemy attacked before the 
crossing operation was completed.  The 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry battled 
with the 230th Legion and steadily advanced against them.
  Out on the left outside flank, the 209th Skeletal Warg Riders were arrayed 
against the 276th Light Cavalry.  The horses of the 276th Light Cavalry were 
spooked by the terrible Beasts they beheld.  On this field, the 276th 
Light Cavalry were held off by earthen ramparts built up by their opponents. 
But the 276th Light Cavalry had a giant worm on retainer to undermine it, 
and the 276th Light Cavalry broke through quickly, demoralizing them.  The 
209th Skeletal Warg Riders battled with the 276th Light Cavalry and were 
slowly bent back by their attack.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Kahn, a final savage 
thrust finished off their enemy and won the day for Guerin.  The 240th 
Skeletal Bowmen demolished the 74th Camel Corps.  The 109th Skeletal 
Heavy Cavalry destroyed the 230th Legion.  The 276th Light Cavalry slew the 
209th Skeletal Warg Riders almost to a man.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons 
pursued the enemy and annihilated the 239th Legion.  The 277th Eagles chased 
after the enemy and scattered the 20th Legion in all directions.  Rejaf was 
overrun by the forces of Guerin.  Rolando (#55) retreated to Kajaani.  
Tiffany (#87) made for the safety of Kajaani with her motley army.
  From Kahn:  In early summer, Tiffany marched into Rejaf from Kajaani to 
defend Rejaf against its would-be conquerors.


END MOVES REPORT

